    tags: ["faq", "zebron quizzes", "zebron courses", "certifications", "test center", "organization admin"],
    content: "Quick answers for organization admins, owners and managers. Where there's more to read, the answer names the full article.\n\n# Settings\n\n## How do I change our organization's color, background or logo?\n\nOpen **Settings** from your dashboard (owners and admins), then **Appearance → Show**. Pick a color and a page background and press **Save**, or **Upload logo** (PNG, JPEG or WebP up to 5 MB). Every page of your organization uses them. See \"Organization branding: color, background and logo\".\n\n## Can members reach their training group from the dashboard?\n\nYes. Members of a training group see **Your training group(s)** on the dashboard, with a link to each group and their next assignments.\n\n## Where are my applications' settings?\n\nOpen **Administration** from your dashboard. Under **Application settings** there is one link per application you can manage: **Learning administration**, **Test Center**, **Knowledge Center** and **Blog**. They open the same pages as the **gear** on each dashboard card. You only see the applications your organization uses and that your role can manage.\n\n# Test Center\n\n## How do I add a Zebron quiz to my organization's Test Center?\n\nLink it to one of your programs:\n\n1. Click the **gear** on the **Test Center** card of your dashboard, or open **Administration → Application settings → Test Center**.\n2. In **Structure**, click **✎** on one of your programs, or create one with **New program**.\n3. Under **Zebron quizzes in this program**, tick the quizzes you want and press **Save Changes**.\n\nYour learners then see the quiz in their **Quiz Library**, marked **Zebron**. You can link up to 50 Zebron quizzes per program. See \"Managing Test Center programs, quizzes, topics and questions\".\n\n## Can I edit a Zebron quiz's questions?\n\nNo. Zebron quizzes are shared with every organization and stay read-only. To change questions, create your own quiz in one of your programs and add or import questions there.\n\n## How do I stop offering a Zebron quiz?\n\nUntick it in the program and save, or make the program inactive. Your members' past results are kept.\n\n## Can I delete a quiz?\n\nYes, your own quizzes: in the Test Center settings, ⋮ → **Delete quiz**. It's blocked while a course uses the quiz as its final exam, and learner results are kept. To hide a quiz without losing it, untick **Quiz is active**. Zebron quizzes can't be deleted by organizations; untick them in your program instead.\n\n## Can members take Zebron quizzes I haven't linked?\n\nYes, on Zebron's own pages at **/test-center/quizzes**, with any signed-in account. Those results are personal and don't appear in your organization's results.\n\n# Courses\n\n## How do I offer Zebron courses to my members?\n\nYour members see only your own courses until you choose Zebron ones:\n\n1. Open **Manage courses** in your organization's Courses pages.\n2. Under **Zebron courses for your members**, press **Choose Zebron courses** (admins and owners).\n3. Tick the courses and press **Save**.\n\nSee \"Building a course\", section \"Zebron courses on your organization's pages\".\n\n## A member started a Zebron course we don't offer. Do they lose their progress?\n\nNo. Their progress is kept and **My learning** opens the course on Zebron's own pages (/courses).\n\n## Can I assign a Zebron course to members?\n\nNot yet. **Assign** covers your organization's own courses only.\n\n## Why can't I publish my course?\n\nThe builder lists what's missing under **Before you publish**: a title, at least one lesson, content in every lesson, complete quick checks and https links. If the course has a final exam, its quiz must be marked **Exam only**; otherwise learners could practise the same questions with the answers shown. Tick **Exam only** on the quiz in Test Center → Structure, or choose another quiz.\n\n## How do I delete a course?\n\nPress **Delete** next to the course on **Manage courses**, or use **⋮ → Delete course** in the builder. A confirmation shows first. Managers, admins and owners delete any course; staff delete only drafts and courses in review. Deleting can't be undone, so **⋮ → Unpublish** is safer if you may need the course again.\n\n## A member removed a course from My learning. Can it be recovered?\n\nYes, they did not lose anything. Their progress is kept: they open **Removed courses** on My learning and press **Put back**, or simply continue the course. Courses you assigned still show under **Assigned to you**.\n\n# Certifications\n\n## Why don't my members see Zebron or external certifications?\n\nOn your organization's pages, members see only your own certifications until an admin or owner switches the other catalogues on. Open **Certifications** from your organization and tick **Zebron Certifications** and/or **External Professional Certifications** under **Certifications your members see**. See \"Certifications\", section \"On your organization's pages\".\n\n## Do members need the Zebron courses in a certification to be offered too?\n\nNo. If a course inside a Zebron certification isn't offered by your organization, it opens on Zebron's own pages, and progress still counts.\n\n# Training Groups\n\n## How do I separate bootcamp cohorts?\n\nUse **Training Groups**. Request it under **Administration → Contract → Learning**, then create a group per cohort, choose its leads and instructors, and add members. See \"Training Groups: cohorts, leads and rosters\".\n\n## Can a manager control only their own cohort?\n\nYes. Managers can edit and manage members only of groups where they are a **lead**. Admins and owners manage every group.\n\n## Can I assign a course to a whole cohort?\n\nYes. Open the group and press **Assign a course**. Everyone in the group gets it, people who join later get it too, and people who are withdrawn lose it unless they've finished it. See \"Training Groups: cohorts, leads and rosters\", section \"Assigning courses to a group\".\n\n## What happens when a cohort ends?\n\nThe group is **locked** (no member or course changes; an admin can **Reopen** it), a **completion summary** is built overnight with a CSV download, and after 30 days the group is **archived**: it leaves the filters and My learning but stays on Training Groups under **Archived**. Nothing is deleted.\n\n## Can I get a cohort report?\n\nYes. Open the group and press **Download PDF** for details, courses, members and each member's progress in each course. The completion summary and member list are also available as CSV.\n\n## Can students sign up for our bootcamp themselves?\n\nYes, without opening up your organization. Set the group's **Enrollment** to **Application**, add questions if you like, and share the join link. Applicants need a Zebron account; when you approve them they get an invitation to your organization and join the group when they accept. Use **Request to join** for existing members, and turn on the **waitlist** to fill places automatically.\n\n## Why can't I add more people to a group?\n\nThe group is at its **Capacity**, it's cancelled, or the person isn't an active member of your organization. Raise the capacity under **Edit** or invite the person first.\n\n# Who can change what\n\n| Setting | Who |\n| --- | --- |\n| Link Zebron quizzes, Test Center structure | Managers, admins, owners |\n| Create, publish, assign and delete courses | Managers, admins, owners (staff: drafts) |\n| Choose Zebron courses for members | Admins and owners |\n| Show Zebron or external certifications | Admins and owners |\n| Create training groups | Managers (as lead), admins, owners |\n| Delete training groups | Admins and owners |\n\nStill stuck? Open a ticket from **My Account → Help & Support** on your dashboard, or go to /support.",
