    tags: ["project management", "pmbok", "agile", "safe", "program"],
    content: "The **Project & Agile Delivery Program** collects Zebron courses on delivering projects and products:\n\n1. **Project Management Fundamentals** (beginner, about 2¾ hours)\n2. **SAFe Agile: Scaling Agile with the Scaled Agile Framework** (intermediate, about 2¾ hours)\n\nEach course has a Test Center quiz for practice, and its final exam draws 20 questions from it.\n\n# Project Management Fundamentals\n\nAligned with PMI's **PMBOK® Guide Eighth Edition** (November 2025): six principles, seven performance domains (Governance, Scope, Schedule, Finance, Stakeholders, Resources, Risk) and five focus areas (Initiating, Planning, Executing, Monitoring and Controlling, Closing).\n\n| Module | Topics |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1. Project basics | Projects vs operations, the project manager, predictive, agile and hybrid life cycles |\n| 2. The PMBOK Guide | Principles, performance domains, focus areas and tailoring |\n| 3. Starting a project | Business case and benefits, the charter, stakeholders |\n| 4. Scope and schedule | Requirements and scope creep, the WBS, the critical path |\n| 5. Cost, resources and risk | Estimating (including three-point), budgets and reserves, RACI, risk responses |\n| 6. Executing and leading | Team development, communication planning, quality and procurement |\n| 7. Monitoring and controlling | Earned value (PV, EV, AC, SPI, CPI), change control, status reporting |\n| 8. Closing and next steps | Closure, lessons learned and benefits, certifications and tools |\n\n# SAFe Agile\n\n| Module | Topics |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1. Agile, Lean and SAFe | Why scale Agile, Agile and Lean basics, SAFe configurations, SAFe today |\n| 2. Values and principles | Core values, the ten Lean-Agile principles, Lean-Agile leadership |\n| 3. Agile teams | Roles, iterations and events, stories and estimation |\n| 4. The Agile Release Train | ARTs and Planning Intervals, ART roles, features and WSJF |\n| 5. PI Planning | Purpose and inputs, the two-day agenda, ROAM and the confidence vote |\n| 6. Executing the PI | Syncs, system demo, IP iteration, Inspect and Adapt, the Continuous Delivery Pipeline |\n| 7. Portfolio and large solutions | Value streams, Lean Portfolio Management and epics, Solution Trains |\n| 8. Measuring and adopting SAFe | Flow metrics, implementation and pitfalls, AI-Native SAFe |\n\n> These are independent Zebron courses, not affiliated with or endorsed by PMI or Scaled Agile, Inc., and they don't grant PMI or SAFe certifications. PMI, PMBOK, CAPM and PMP are registered marks of the Project Management Institute, Inc. SAFe® and Scaled Agile Framework® are registered trademarks of Scaled Agile, Inc.\n\n# For Zebron administrators\n\nContent: `scripts/agile-program/`. Seed it with `node scripts/seed-agile-program.mjs --check`, then `--apply` (add `--overwrite` to replace; learner progress is kept). Courses are ordered by their `order` field; add new ones as more files in the same folder.",
