    tags: ["aws", "cloud practitioner", "ai practitioner", "certification", "exam prep", "program"],
    content: "The **AWS Certification Prep** program prepares learners for two foundational AWS certifications. Each has an exam prep course and an exam-prep certification with a full practice exam:\n\n| Course | Exam | Domains |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **AWS Cloud Practitioner (CLF-C02) Exam Prep** (24 lessons, 81 practice questions) | AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner (CLF-C02) | Cloud Concepts 24%, Security and Compliance 30%, Cloud Technology and Services 34%, Billing, Pricing, and Support 12% |\n| **AWS AI Practitioner (AIF-C01) Exam Prep** (24 lessons, 80 practice questions) | AWS Certified AI Practitioner (AIF-C01) | Fundamentals of AI and ML 20%, Fundamentals of Generative AI 24%, Applications of Foundation Models 28%, Guidelines for Responsible AI 14%, Security, Compliance, and Governance for AI Solutions 14% |\n\n# How it works\n\n1. Take the course. Every lesson maps to an official task statement in AWS's exam guide, and each Test Center topic matches a task statement (for example \"2.3 Access management\").\n2. Pass the course final exam (20 questions drawn from the course quiz).\n3. Open the certification (Test Center, Certifications) to see the task-statement map and take the **practice exam**: 65 questions in 90 minutes, weighted by the official domains, with an estimated score on AWS's 100–1,000 scale (700 to pass).\n4. When you pass, you're marked **Exam ready**; book the real exam with AWS.\n\n# What the courses cover\n\n**Cloud Practitioner**: cloud benefits, the Well-Architected Framework, migration and the Cloud Adoption Framework, cloud economics, the shared responsibility model, IAM, security and compliance services, global infrastructure, compute, storage, databases, networking, AI/ML and analytics services, pricing models, billing tools and AWS Support.\n\n**AI Practitioner**: AI, ML and deep learning, AWS AI services, the ML lifecycle, generative AI concepts and limitations, Amazon Bedrock, SageMaker AI and JumpStart, Amazon Quick, Kiro, Strands Agents and Amazon Bedrock AgentCore, RAG, inference parameters, prompt engineering and prompt risks, fine-tuning, evaluation metrics, responsible AI, transparency, and AI security and governance.\n\n> Zebron is not affiliated with or endorsed by Amazon Web Services. AWS and related marks are trademarks of Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. The exams are taken through AWS, not on Zebron.\n\n# For Zebron administrators\n\nContent: `scripts/aws-program/` (courses, and `track.mjs` with the domains and task-statement map). Seed it with `node scripts/seed-aws-certification-prep.mjs --check`, then `--apply` (add `--overwrite` to replace; learner progress is kept). When AWS publishes a new exam version, update the domains, weights and task statements in `track.mjs` and the matching lessons.",
